.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt NL80211 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nl80211
.Nd the generic netlink family that drives a Wi-Fi station
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/socket.h
.In linux/netlink.h
.In linux/genetlink.h
.In linux/nl80211.h
.Ft int
.Fn socket "AF_NETLINK" "SOCK_RAW" "NETLINK_GENERIC"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the generic netlink family through which
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
and
.Xr iw 8
scan, join and leave Wi-Fi networks.
Its commands, attributes and numbers are those of Linux's
.In linux/nl80211.h ,
version 1, with no private header.
Resolve the family and its multicast groups by name through
.Ql nlctrl ,
as
.Xr genetlink 7
describes.
.Pp
Each radio is a wiphy, numbered from 0 and named
.Ql phyN ,
with one station interface, such as
.Ql wlan0 .
A request names its interface by
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_IFINDEX
or by
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_WDEV ,
whose value is the wiphy's number shifted left 32 bits, plus one.
A request that names neither fails with
.Er EINVAL ;
one that names an interface or wiphy not present fails with
.Er ENODEV .
The radios belong to the first network namespace: from another, a request
that names one fails with
.Er ENODEV
and a dump lists none.
Commands that change the station need network administration privilege and
otherwise fail with
.Er EPERM .
A request runs on the kernel's wireless worker and its acknowledgement comes
once the station has taken it; an outcome that comes later, such as the
access point's answer, comes as an event.
.Sh GROUPS
.Bl -tag -width regulatory
.It Ql config
Not used; present for programs that join it.
.It Ql scan
.Dv TRIGGER_SCAN
when a scan begins,
.Dv NEW_SCAN_RESULTS
when it ends and
.Dv SCAN_ABORTED
when it is aborted.
A scan this family started carries its SSIDs, channels, elements and flags;
another carries its interface alone.
.It Ql regulatory
.Dv REG_CHANGE ,
with
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_REG_ALPHA2
and the domain's type.
.It Ql mlme
.Dv AUTHENTICATE ,
.Dv ASSOCIATE ,
.Dv DEAUTHENTICATE ,
.Dv DISASSOCIATE ,
their
.Dv UNPROT_
forms,
.Dv CONNECT ,
.Dv DISCONNECT ,
.Dv MICHAEL_MIC_FAILURE
and
.Dv FRAME_TX_STATUS .
The first two carry the access point's frame in
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_FRAME ,
or
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_TIMED_OUT
and its address when no answer came.
.It Ql vendor
Not used.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width GET_PROTOCOL_FEATURES
.It Dv GET_PROTOCOL_FEATURES
Reports
.Dv NL80211_PROTOCOL_FEATURE_SPLIT_WIPHY_DUMP .
.It Dv GET_WIPHY
Describes a wiphy: the supported interface types (station only), commands,
cipher suites (TKIP, CCMP and BIP-CMAC-128), the 2.4 GHz band with its
channels, rates and HT capabilities, the scan limits, the frame types a
station sends and takes, and
.Dv NL80211_FEATURE_SAE .
A request by
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_WIPHY ,
.Dv IFINDEX
or
.Dv WDEV
answers in one message.
A dump lists every wiphy, or the one the request names; with
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_SPLIT_WIPHY_DUMP
it sends each in four messages.
.It Dv GET_INTERFACE
Describes an interface: its name, type, wiphy, wireless device, address and,
while associated, its channel and SSID.
A dump lists every interface, or those of one wiphy.
.It Dv SET_INTERFACE
Accepts the station type; another type or four-address mode is
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
.It Dv TRIGGER_SCAN
Scans for up to 4 SSIDs, an empty one for any, on the channels named, or on
every enabled channel, with up to 512 bytes of elements for the probe
requests.
A disabled channel is left out, and a request left with none is
.Er EINVAL .
.Dv NL80211_SCAN_FLAG_FLUSH
removes, at the end, the entries the scan did not hear; another flag is
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
A scan already running is
.Er EBUSY .
.It Dv ABORT_SCAN
Aborts the running scan;
.Er ENOENT
when none runs.
.It Dv GET_SCAN
Dumps the BSS table: address, channel, signal in mBm, TSF, beacon interval,
capability, elements and age, and
.Dv NL80211_BSS_STATUS
for the access point the station is with.
Entries not heard for 30 s leave the table first.
.It Dv AUTHENTICATE
Authenticates with a BSS of the table by Open System, or by SAE with the
frame's fields in
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_AUTH_DATA .
Shared Key, FT, FILS, WEP keys and a change of local state alone are
refused.
.It Dv ASSOCIATE
Associates with the BSS authenticated with, or reassociates from
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_PREV_BSSID ,
sending the request's elements, of up to 1024 bytes.
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_CONTROL_PORT
keeps the port closed to all but EAPOL until
.Dv SET_STATION
authorizes it.
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_USE_MFP
is either none or required.
.It Dv DEAUTHENTICATE , Dv DISASSOCIATE
Leave the access point with a nonzero reason;
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_LOCAL_STATE_CHANGE
sends no frame.
.It Dv CONNECT
Joins an SSID, at
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_MAC
and on
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_WIPHY_FREQ
when they are given: it scans when the table has no such BSS, chooses the
strongest, authenticates by Open System and associates.
The
.Dv CONNECT
event gives the outcome, with
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_TIMEOUT_REASON
when no BSS was found or no answer came.
A connection already under way is
.Er EALREADY .
SAE needs
.Dv AUTHENTICATE .
.It Dv DISCONNECT
Ends a connection under way or leaves the network;
.Er ENOTCONN
when there is neither.
.It Dv NEW_KEY , Dv SET_KEY , Dv DEL_KEY
Install, select or remove a key, nested in
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_KEY
or in the older top-level attributes.
Pairwise keys have index 0 or 1 and name their peer, group keys 0 to 3 and
integrity keys 4 or 5.
.Dv NL80211_KEY_SEQ
gives the receive counter, at most 6 bytes, least significant first.
.It Dv SET_STATION
Opens or closes the port to the access point through
.Dv NL80211_STA_FLAG_AUTHORIZED
in
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_STA_FLAGS2 ;
another flag is
.Er EINVAL .
.It Dv GET_STATION
Describes the access point: signal, byte and packet counts, retries and
failures, inactive and connected time, beacon loss, rates and flags.
The counts start at the association and take in every frame sent to the
access point, management and null frames among them.
Another address is
.Er ENOENT .
.It Dv GET_SURVEY
Dumps the operating channel with its noise.
.It Dv GET_REG
Gives the world domain,
.Ql 00 .
.It Dv REGISTER_FRAME
Delivers action frames whose body begins with
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_FRAME_MATCH ,
of up to 64 bytes, to this socket as
.Dv FRAME
messages.
A match that is a prefix of another's, or that has another's as its prefix,
is
.Er EALREADY .
Registrations end when the socket closes.
.It Dv FRAME
Sends an action frame on
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_WIPHY_FREQ
or the operating channel.
The reply carries the
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_COOKIE
that its
.Dv FRAME_TX_STATUS
event names, unless
.Dv NL80211_ATTR_DONT_WAIT_FOR_ACK
asked for neither.
.It Dv GET_POWER_SAVE , Dv SET_POWER_SAVE
Power save is always off; turning it on is
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
.El
.Pp
Every other command is
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
.Sh LIMITS
There is no connection-quality monitor, so
.Dv SET_CQM
is
.Er EOPNOTSUPP
and
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8 Ns 's
background scan polls
.Dv GET_STATION
instead.
There is no 5 GHz band, no access-point mode, no off-channel wait for
.Dv FRAME ,
no WEP and no extended key ID.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr genetlink 7 ,
.Xr netlink 7 ,
.Xr iw 8 ,
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
